# Optimization Techniques for Data Science and Cybersecurity

A collection of two practical projects developed for the **Optimization Techniques for Data Science and Cybersecurity** course, as part of the Master's Degree in **Data Science and Innovation Management**.

**Team project:** the two assignments were completed collaboratively by a group of four students — myself and three female classmates.

## Projects

| Project | Topic | Main concepts |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Project 1 — Numerical Optimization](Project%201/) | Classical and proximal optimization methods | Gradient descent, Armijo line search, Newton, BFGS, LASSO, ISTA, FISTA |
| [Project 2 — Optimization for Machine Learning](Project%202/) | Neural network training and model comparison | Backpropagation, SGD, Momentum, Nesterov, RMSProp, Adam, logistic regression, SVM |

Each folder includes the Python implementations, experimental analyses and available figures or CSV outputs. See the project-specific `README.md` files for details and execution instructions.

## Tools

- Python
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- SciPy (optional, for an additional check in Project 1)

